---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/15-03/', docs='https://noldus.com/shared/resources/book/noldus-product-documentation/chapter/catwalk-xt/page/catwalk-xt-107-technical-specifications', oem='https://mescalero.noldus.com/storage/images/catwalk-xt-hardware-20240412163951.webp', installed='https://en-facilities.szbl.ac.cn/uploads/51378026_1742524989.jpg';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Noldus CatWalk XT 10.7 · stationary exterior and detached shape card" description="Orbit a closed documentary frame and compare original abstract geometric artwork marks." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment cw"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/15-03/">← Equipment 15-03</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#cw-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">15-03 · STATIONARY EXTERIOR & DETACHED ARTWORK / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Noldus CatWalk XT 10.7</h2><p>Orbit the stationary exterior. On the separate teaching display, measure three abstract artwork marks: a rectangle, a diamond, and three collinear points that enclose no area. The marks were drawn by hand in software and do not represent animals or experimental data.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Fixed geometry, no instruments operating</h3><div id="cw-view" aria-label="Orbitable stationary CatWalk frame, capped dark upper housing, and separately positioned artwork display"></div>
<div class="bar"><button data-cw-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-cw-view="shell">Frame detail</button><button data-cw-view="display">Detached display</button><button id="cw-cycle">Next artwork mark</button></div>
<p id="cw-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal badge switches the drawn shape on the detached display. The exterior stays fixed.</p></section>
<section><h3>Detached ink mark geometry</h3><canvas id="cw-plot" width="660" height="450" aria-label="Synthetic two-dimensional ink mark using fixed millimeter coordinates"></canvas>
<div class="fields"><label>Artwork mark<select id="cw-case"><option value="rectangle">Rectangular ink stamp</option><option value="diamond">Offset diamond stamp</option><option value="collinear">Collinear marks</option></select></label></div>
<div class="bar"><button class="primary" id="cw-inspect">Inspect mark geometry</button><button id="cw-reset">Reset</button></div><p id="cw-status" aria-live="polite">Choose an abstract mark and inspect its polygon.</p><output id="cw-result"></output><div class="bar"><button id="cw-json" disabled>Inspection JSON</button></div></section></div>
<section id="cw-evidence"><h3>Geometry and evidence</h3><p>Selected configuration: CatWalk XT generation 10.7, shown as a fixed outer frame without accessory boxes. <a href={docs}>Noldus version-specific documentation</a> gives a 130 × 68 × 152 cm frame envelope. The <a href={oem}>Noldus series photograph</a> and the <a href={installed}>Shenzhen Bay Laboratory installation photo</a> establish the wheeled extrusion frame and upper cover silhouettes; pose and trim are visually inferred, not calibrated to an installation. Glass and open sections are represented by solid opaque stand-ins. The small lower housing is a blank appearance marker, not an imaging component.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original render showing the black rolling frame next to an independent monitor"/><figcaption>Original whole model render. Caster arrangement, extrusion stand and black upper cover are documentary; appearance is not a measured installation.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="660" height="440" src={base+'detail.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original rendering of a static opaque upper panel and stationary frame"/><figcaption>Original upper detail. The pale outer panel is fixed and opaque, with no imaging geometry or control.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Independent reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>10.7 frame envelope</td><td>130 × 68 × 152 cm</td><td>Verified metric length × depth × height, excluding the separate artwork display.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rectangle and diamond paper marks</td><td>24×16 mm rectangle; diamond diagonals 30 and 20 mm</td><td>384 and 300 mm²; the diamond centroid is (6,4) mm.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Collinear paper marks</td><td>Zero enclosed area</td><td>Area = 0; area centroid and filled perimeter are null.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Original register acceptance</td><td>Replay of animal foot contacts</td><td>Not implemented or run. No acquisition, tracking, animal placement, behavior or experimental workflow.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The unrelated polygon uses the signed shoelace cross products for area and the cross-product-weighted centroid. X points right and Y points up, in millimeters. The JSON export holds the fixed art sheet and mark IDs, unaltered corner coordinates, units and provenance. It contains no recorded footprints, sequence, stride, animal data or camera output.</p>
<p><a href={base+'catwalk-xt-107-static.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'mark-example.json'}>Output schema example</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No headset or live hardware was tested.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/15-03/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.cw{max-width:76rem}.cw .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.cw section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.cw .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.44rem;margin:.55rem 0}.cw .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.48rem}.cw label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.2rem;font-size:.92rem}.cw input,.cw select,.cw button{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.cw button{cursor:pointer}.cw button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.cw .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.cw #cw-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,435px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.cw #cw-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.cw #cw-plot,.cw img{width:100%;height:auto}.cw #cw-result{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.45rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.cw #cw-status.error{color:#a54a34}.cw .scroll{overflow:auto}.cw table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.cw td,.cw th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.cw figure{margin:.8rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.cw .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
